        openingHook: ['He doesn’t leave them with a memory. He promises another Comforter. This is not a lecture for somebody else. It is for the week you actually have.', 'The Spirit stays. That is the gift. This is not a lecture for somebody else. It is for the week you actually have.'],
        context: ['Jesus is hours from leaving. The disciples are about to feel the absence. He says he will pray the Father, and the Father will give another Comforter, that he may abide with you for ever. Not a visit. An abiding. That is why this passage still belongs in a class that wants more than a slogan.', 'Another Comforter means one of the same kind as Jesus, not a thinner substitute. The Spirit is how the Father keeps his people when the visible Jesus is no longer in the room. That is why this passage still belongs in a class that wants more than a slogan.'],
        points: [
          { heading: ['Hear what God already said', 'Start with the Word, not the week'], thought: ['He doesn’t leave them with a memory. He promises another Comforter. That line is not a slogan. It is the doorway into the text.', 'The Spirit stays. That is the gift. That line is not a slogan. It is the doorway into the text.'] },
          { heading: ['See where the passage sits', 'The story behind the sentence'], thought: ['Jesus is hours from leaving. Stay there long enough for the room to quiet down.', 'Another Comforter means one of the same kind as Jesus, not a thinner substitute. Stay there long enough for the room to quiet down.'] },
          { heading: ['Take the next obedient step', 'Leave with one clear yes'], thought: ['Ask the Father. Then walk as someone who is not alone. The Comforter was promised for ever.', 'Jesus’ message is direct: he shall give you another Comforter, that he may abide with you for ever. Don’t live like an orphan.'] },
        ],
        application: ['Most of us live as if we were alone with a Bible and a memory. When the room feels empty. When we try to obey without help. When we treat the Spirit as a mood we might feel on Sunday. Jesus promised a Person who abides. Power for witness, comfort in the valley, and help to keep his word are not three different gods. They are his presence. Take it deeper: do not leave with the same quiet bargain you walked in with. Let the Word rearrange what you call enough, safe, and later.', 'Don’t reduce the Holy Spirit to a feeling you chase. Ask. Obey. He was given to stay. Take it deeper: do not leave with the same quiet bargain you walked in with. Let the Word rearrange what you call enough, safe, and later.'],
        invitation: ['Brothers, come. Where are you living as if the Comforter left with the closing prayer? The temptation. The witness you’ve avoided. The grief. Maybe a week you are trying to carry without him. If the Spirit is pressing you, do not wait for a better feeling. Answer him.', 'Brothers, come. What would change if you believed he abides, not just visits? Name one place you have locked him out of. If the Spirit is pressing you, do not wait for a better feeling. Answer him.'],
        closingPrayer: ['Father, thank you for your Word. Plant this truth in us for the week we actually have. Give us courage to obey and mercy when we fail. Through Jesus Christ. Amen.', 'Lord, we have heard you. Now keep us from leaving this room unchanged. Make us doers of the Word. In Jesus’ name. Amen.'],
